Body:
@Jandev because Azure Foundry has special requirements we created our own Azure Foundry AI provider. https://github.com/ophiosdev/azure-foundry-provider 

It's easy to use in OpenCode. We always use it our OpenCode container.

https://github.com/ophiosdev/opencode-cli-container

I started tracing this and need a small log to pin the exact trigger before I can land a precise fix.

What I found so far: the notification for the completion sound fires in `packages/tui/src/feature-plugins/system/notifications.ts` on **every** `session.status` busy→idle transition per session (deduped only by a module-local `active` set, so one sound per busy→idle cycle). Server-side, `busy` is re-published at the top of every agent step (path `src/session/processor.ts` / the run loop) and `idle` is published once per completed run. So a repeated idle sound means a session is going busy→idle repeatedly while it looks idle to you — a few candidates: a subagent session completing in the background, a queued/steer prompt re-running, a status that gets stuck `busy`, or the active `session-warming-opt-in` plugin.

To tell them apart, could you capture the actual event timeline? Drop this debug plugin at `~/.config/opencode/plugins/status-log.ts`:

```ts
import { appendFile, mkdir } from "node:fs/promises"
import path from "node:path"

export default {
  id: "debug-status-log",
  async tui(api: any) {
    const file = path.join(process.env.HOME ?? "", ".cache/opencode/status-events.log")
    await mkdir(path.dirname(file), { recursive: true })
    const line = (s: string) => appendFile(file, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${s}\n`).catch(() => {})
    await line("== started ==")

    api.event.on("session.status", (e: any) => {
      const parent = api.state.session.get(e.properties.sessionID)?.parentID
      line(`STATUS ${e.properties.sessionID} parent=${parent ?? "-"} ${JSON.stringify(e.properties.status)}`)
    })
    api.event.on("session.idle", (e: any) => {
      line(`IDLE ${e.properties.sessionID}`)
    })
  },
}
```

Then: 1) start `opencode2`, leave it idle, wait for the sound, 2) quit and paste `~/.cache/opencode/status-events.log`.

What the log tells us:
- `STATUS <id> ... busy` then `... idle` pairs around each sound + the `parent` value → whether it's the top-level session (`done`) or a subagent (`subagent_done`) cycling.
- `busy` with no matching `idle` → a stuck-busy status.
- an empty log while the sound plays → not `session.status`-driven, and I'll look at the audio path instead.

If you could also run once with `session-warming-opt-in` disabled and share both logs, that bisects the most likely trigger.
